[FILES_REFERENCE]
overview: Where to put different types of information
purpose: Route discovered knowledge to correct documentation file
principle: Each file has specific scope - don't mix concerns

[FILE_CLAUDE_MD]
location: /CLAUDE.md (root of project)
scope: Critical universal rules (apply to ALL work on project)
examples_update:
  - "Never use std::cout, use engine_log.h"
  - "No raw delete/new outside RAII"
  - "All C++ code must be snake_case"
  - "Tabs (size 4) for indentation"
examples_not:
  - Layer-specific rules (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Algorithm details (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Module responsibilities (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Memory allocator patterns (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
when_update: Rare. Only if affects ALL code in project.
format: Markdown section under "⚠️ Critical Rules"
size: Keep small (< 500 words total)

[FILE_ARCHITECTURE_TOON]
location: docs/agent/ARCHITECTURE.toon
scope: Layer structure, module interactions, systems, patterns
examples_update:
  - ECS world management and system registration
  - Module lifecycle and service locator pattern
  - Resource system pipeline and caching
  - Descriptor system inheritance and serialization
  - Memory allocator system and usage patterns
  - Render pipeline architecture (extractors, passes, wiring)
examples_not:
  - Code style rules (→ CLAUDE.md)
  - Specific function implementations (read code for that)
  - "Absolute" constraints like "never" (→ separate section if critical)
when_update: When understanding system interactions or design patterns
format: [SECTION_NAME] with structured sub-sections
size: Comprehensive reference document

[FILE_CONSTRAINTS_TOON]
location: docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon
scope: Hard architectural rules and "never/always" statements
examples_update:
  - "Always use frame_allocator for per-frame temporaries"
  - "Never store frame-allocated pointers across frames"
  - "ImGui: always check Begin() return value before End()"
  - "Resources: never bypass cache, always use res::tag"
examples_not:
  - "How to use X" (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Implementation patterns (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Code style (→ CLAUDE.md)
when_update: When discovering hard "must not" or "always must" rules
format: [CONSTRAINT_N] with rule + why + how_to_apply
size: Focused reference (one constraint = 5-10 lines max)

[FILE_CODE_CONVENTIONS_TOON]
location: docs/agent/CODE_CONVENTIONS.toon
scope: Naming, style, architecture patterns specific to codebase
examples_update:
  - Namespace abbreviations (ds, ecs, scn, gui, rnd, res, inp, edt, gs, cfg, wnd)
  - File naming patterns (prefix_name.hpp/.cpp)
  - Component naming (_component suffix)
  - System patterns (ecs::system_interface inheritance)
examples_not:
  - Language-level rules (C++20, no extensions) → CLAUDE.md
  - Logic patterns that change (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
when_update: When discovering consistent naming/style patterns
format: [PATTERN_NAME] sections
size: Reference document

[FILE_QUICK_LINKS_TOON]
location: docs/agent/QUICK_LINKS.toon
scope: Navigation shortcuts to important files and concepts
examples_update:
  - "For ECS questions: Core/core/ecs/"
  - "For rendering: Engine/render/"
  - "For ImGui editor: Editor/panels/"
  - "For resources: Core/core/res/"
examples_not:
  - Deep architectural explanations (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Rules and constraints (→ CONSTRAINTS.toon)
when_update: When discovering important directory structure
format: [SECTION] → file/folder descriptions
size: Quick index

[DECISION_MATRIX]
Information Type → File

Universal rule (affects all code)
  → CLAUDE.md

Hard "never/always" constraint
  → CONSTRAINTS.toon

System design / architecture / interactions
  → ARCHITECTURE.toon

Code naming / style / patterns
  → CODE_CONVENTIONS.toon

File locations / quick navigation
  → QUICK_LINKS.toon

Unknown file → Ask or check FILES_REFERENCE.toon (this file)
